api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sanity-io/sdk/commit/aa2c3f7fc0fd123ea92b2bae967f648c231f16f6","node_id":"C_kwDONHsbrtoAKGFhMmMzZjdmYzBmZDEyM2VhOTJiMmJhZTk2N2Y2NDhjMjMxZjE2ZjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sanity-io/sdk/commit/d764d354fc85b8ffcdd41cf86f280294a28c1d71","sha":"d764d354fc85b8ffcdd41cf86f280294a28c1d71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sanity-io/sdk/commits/d764d354fc85b8ffcdd41cf86f280294a28c1d71"}],"sha":"aa2c3f7fc0fd123ea92b2bae967f648c231f16f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sanity-io/sdk/commits/aa2c3f7fc0fd123ea92b2bae967f648c231f16f6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2244375?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gu-stav/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gu-stav/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gu-stav/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gu-stav/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gu-stav","id":2244375,"login":"gu-stav","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDQzNzU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gu-stav/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gu-stav/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gu-stav/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gu-stav/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gu-stav/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gu-stav","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sanity-io/sdk/commits/d764d354fc85b8ffcdd41cf86f280294a28c1d71/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T12:11:25Z","email":"gu@stav.dev","name":"Gustav Hansen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T12:11:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(core): scope a failed document read to the document it belongs to (#1280)\n\n* fix(core): scope a failed document read to its own document\n\nOne document store is created per resource, and its per-document listen\nstreams were merged into a single subscription. A read that failed took that\nsubscription down and landed in a store-wide error, which the selectors threw\nbefore looking at the document that was asked for. One document the reader may\nnot read therefore failed every document in the same project and dataset, for\ngood and without a retry.\n\nThe error is now recorded against the document it belongs to, so the readers\nof the other documents are unaffected.\n\n* docs(changeset): clarify inaccessible document impact\n\n* fix(core): keep the document error check out of the selectors\n\nThe two selectors read the same per-document error, and adding that read to\neach of them pushed both over the complexity gate. One shared check restores\nthem to the complexity they had before.\n\nThe remaining breach on those selectors and on the test harness is recorded in\nthe health baseline: a whitespace-only change to either file on main reports\nthe same numbers, so it predates this branch.\n\n* fix(core): read a document error from every id the selector reads\n\nA read that is not live-edit resolves a draft and a published document, and it\nreturns early while either is missing. The error was only ever read from the\nrequested id, so an inaccessible draft left the document loading forever with\nnothing thrown, and left the sync status reporting a document as synced.\n\nEach selector now reads the error from every id it resolves.\n\n* refactor(core): resolve the ids a document read depends on in one place\n\nBoth selectors worked out the draft, published and version ids for themselves,\nand reading the per-document error from each of them pushed both over the\ncomplexity gate. One shared resolver leaves each selector reading a list of ids\nit is handed, which takes them under the gate on their own rather than through\na baseline entry.\n\n* fix(core): resolve a document read in one pass over its ids\n\nThe error check was added to each selector in turn, which pushed both over the\ncomplexity gate, and the gate was answered with a baseline entry rather than\nwith simpler code.\n\nEach selector now asks for the ids a read resolves and walks them once, taking\nthe error, the missing read and the winning document from the same pass. That\ndrops the branching the gate objected to, so the baseline no longer records\nthese functions.\n\n* fix(core): fail a write to a document that could not be read\n\nA read error used to reach the store-wide error, which the write path watches,\nso an edit to a document the reader may not read rejected. Recording the error\non the document alone took that away: the transaction waited for a document\nthat never loads, the caller never settled, and everything queued behind it\nwaited too.\n\nA queued transaction whose document carries a read error now fails with it,\nwhich the existing action-error path already reports and unqueues.\n\n* fix(core): read a document again after a transient failure\n\nLatching every error on the document meant one timeout, rate limit or 5xx\nblanked it until nothing was subscribed to it any more. The listen retry only\never recovered from being out of sync.\n\nIt now makes the same split the dataset ACL read makes: retry 408, 429 and 5xx\nwith the backoff already used here, and latch what will keep failing.\n\n* fix(core): fail a release action on a release it cannot read\n\nA release action carries a release id rather than a document id, so the queued\ntransaction check skipped it while the reducer still waited on the release\ndocument. An unreadable release held back everything queued behind it.\n\nTwo neighbouring reads of the same state go with it: an error is now looked for\nacross every id before any of them is called still loading, so an id that has\nyet to arrive cannot hide one that already failed; and a failed apply of a\nremote document stays a store fault rather than being recorded as though the\ndocument could not be read.\n\n* chore(core): drop comments that restate the code\n\n* fix(core): keep the read failure as the cause of the action error\n\n* fix(core): give up on a read that keeps failing\n\nRetrying a transient failure without a bound turned a lasting 5xx into the\nloading state that never ends, which is the failure this branch set out to\nremove. The retry now stops after a set number of attempts and the error\nlands on the document.\n\n* fix(core): spend the retry budget per failure, not per listener\n\nA listener lives as long as the document is open, so a bounded retry without\nresetOnSuccess counted failures hours apart against one budget. A connection\nthat went out of sync often enough over a session would stop recovering and\nstart throwing at whoever was editing it.\n\n* docs(core): the listener retry budget counts retries, not attempts\n\n* docs(changeset): note the hooks that now throw\n\n* refactor(core): resolve document ids in one place\n\n`failTransactionOnUnreadableDocument` has to cover exactly the ids\n`applyFirstQueuedTransaction` blocks on. They were resolved by two separate\ncopies of the same logic, so any drift would silently put a write back to\nhanging.","tree":{"sha":"cd5ace476e25cfd15fe3f6377b14573386abeece","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sanity-io/sdk/git/trees/cd5ace476e25cfd15fe3f6377b14573386abeece"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sanity-io/sdk/git/commits/d764d354fc85b8ffcdd41cf86f280294a28c1d71","verification":{"payload":"tree cd5ace476e25cfd15fe3f6377b14573386abeece\nparent 1ea6b4a251f4ec701e7044c9043613368440048a\nauthor Gustav Hansen <gu@stav.dev> 1790079085 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790079085 +0200\n\nfix(core): scope a failed document read to the document it belongs to (#1280)\n\n* fix(core): scope a failed document read to its own document\n\nOne document store is created per resource, and its per-document listen\nstreams were merged into a single subscription. A read that failed took that\nsubscription down and landed in a store-wide error, which the selectors threw\nbefore looking at the document that was asked for. One document the reader may\nnot read therefore failed every document in the same project and dataset, for\ngood and without a retry.\n\nThe error is now recorded against the document it belongs to, so the readers\nof the other documents are unaffected.\n\n* docs(changeset): clarify inaccessible document impact\n\n* fix(core): keep the document error check out of the selectors\n\nThe two selectors read the same per-document error, and adding that read to\neach of them pushed both over the complexity gate. One shared check restores\nthem to the complexity they had before.\n\nThe remaining breach on those selectors and on the test harness is recorded in\nthe health baseline: a whitespace-only change to either file on main reports\nthe same numbers, so it predates this branch.\n\n* fix(core): read a document error from every id the selector reads\n\nA read that is not live-edit resolves a draft and a published document, and it\nreturns early while either is missing. The error was only ever read from the\nrequested id, so an inaccessible draft left the document loading forever with\nnothing thrown, and left the sync status reporting a document as synced.\n\nEach selector now reads the error from every id it resolves.\n\n* refactor(core): resolve the ids a document read depends on in one place\n\nBoth selectors worked out the draft, published and version ids for themselves,\nand reading the per-document error from each of them pushed both over the\ncomplexity gate. One shared resolver leaves each selector reading a list of ids\nit is handed, which takes them under the gate on their own rather than through\na baseline entry.\n\n* fix(core): resolve a document read in one pass over its ids\n\nThe error check was added to each selector in turn, which pushed both over the\ncomplexity gate, and the gate was answered with a baseline entry rather than\nwith simpler code.\n\nEach selector now asks for the ids a read resolves and walks them once, taking\nthe error, the missing read and the winning document from the same pass. That\ndrops the branching the gate objected to, so the baseline no longer records\nthese functions.\n\n* fix(core): fail a write to a document that could not be read\n\nA read error used to reach the store-wide error, which the write path watches,\nso an edit to a document the reader may not read rejected. Recording the error\non the document alone took that away: the transaction waited for a document\nthat never loads, the caller never settled, and everything queued behind it\nwaited too.\n\nA queued transaction whose document carries a read error now fails with it,\nwhich the existing action-error path already reports and unqueues.\n\n* fix(core): read a document again after a transient failure\n\nLatching every error on the document meant one timeout, rate limit or 5xx\nblanked it until nothing was subscribed to it any more. The listen retry only\never recovered from being out of sync.\n\nIt now makes the same split the dataset ACL read makes: retry 408, 429 and 5xx\nwith the backoff already used here, and latch what will keep failing.\n\n* fix(core): fail a release action on a release it cannot read\n\nA release action carries a release id rather than a document id, so the queued\ntransaction check skipped it while the reducer still waited on the release\ndocument. An unreadable release held back everything queued behind it.\n\nTwo neighbouring reads of the same state go with it: an error is now looked for\nacross every id before any of them is called still loading, so an id that has\nyet to arrive cannot hide one that already failed; and a failed apply of a\nremote document stays a store fault rather than being recorded as though the\ndocument could not be read.\n\n* chore(core): drop comments that restate the code\n\n* fix(core): keep the read failure as the cause of the action error\n\n* fix(core): give up on a read that keeps failing\n\nRetrying a transient failure without a bound turned a lasting 5xx into the\nloading state that never ends, which is the failure this branch set out to\nremove. The retry now stops after a set number of attempts and the error\nlands on the document.\n\n* fix(core): spend the retry budget per failure, not per listener\n\nA listener lives as long as the document is open, so a bounded retry without\nresetOnSuccess counted failures hours apart against one budget. A connection\nthat went out of sync often enough over a session would stop recovering and\nstart throwing at whoever was editing it.\n\n* docs(core): the listener retry budget counts retries, not attempts\n\n* docs(changeset): note the hooks that now throw\n\n* refactor(core): resolve document ids in one place\n\n`failTransactionOnUnreadableDocument` has to cover exactly the ids\n`applyFirstQueuedTransaction` blocks on. They were resolved by two separate\ncopies of the same logic, so any drift would silently put a write back to\nhanging.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsnBtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiEkQAJAzqkAu1qeXyDEq8X7saDdR\nLILqCFjc3NZDNh69sCBju6wbRKgyK05X8fYKUQpeLuQQRzUDTgc068zp8iF+wWTc\nrVYF/vlV9XhbUQjlOf7oW7wM11qoTH5ITZLJCy6oiYlc6ZK7AVXhLSefATF+rLaT\nYUKU08DDGMkNHkd+C9cgT60cVEKHpc5HbkDnmIzB1Op2RitZmpVszbLLRwtZC5eM\nDdZ3JInJWDA9/EznUMI3weEcW46boIv0T12/O+ktbNBHwl/MNWaCkXKOESh0F3jL\n3gLlISNkaA+fpU+LMqO5r4pz70UU2+E1MV693iPUGg9Ai4GQbsv+eOynMuryFGiw\nJVriC0PEZN9w1q1+aqMPqYcLxp8l3rD+DbStcDwIIsfcSGLBhGvfiVvPb6OVZ8hY\n1fgwn5E4VcPzUM2Rasm+5NS0cCTa5a0dDEix1AS7ZLPaN+DLGijonzTsuDXsS0jx\nHNJHQCJns2PV7NPumN8HPvWj8omiEeGnPe9vasIAER0YsFO4QiA7A1A+x9c/NGup\nbhQURzaqJeWopPBVoX5gmWgIQ70a0sHTxj2yUx+7RCkc8DoN8R46sTRea6RJEohO\nb2TS40wL+uOMTwsYucE/WvYCtfUtHIdryp7UvsZO2gAMVdcVefUACXnPoK/c0PxG\ntfPc16MYXPaLY0twGvGh\n=YYxw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T12:11:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sanity-io/sdk/commit/d764d354fc85b8ffcdd41cf86f280294a28c1d71","node_id":"C_kwDONHsbrtoAKGQ3NjRkMzU0ZmM4NWI4ZmZjZGQ0MWNmODZmMjgwMjk0YTI4YzFkNzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sanity-io/sdk/commit/1ea6