4a04a062db7eb8d8d17000"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38444032?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ariel-gallardo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ariel-gallardo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ariel-gallardo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ariel-gallardo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ariel-gallardo","id":38444032,"login":"ariel-gallardo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NDQ0MDMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ariel-gallardo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ariel-gallardo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ariel-gallardo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ariel-gallardo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ariel-gallardo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ariel-gallardo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ariel-gallardo/restaurante/commits/67bc76ea6af87ecc6afcce965f053456cf293472/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-14T18:18:52Z","email":"38444032+ariel-gallardo@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ariel Gallardo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-14T18:18:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Feat/nx angular (#24)\n\n* feat(dev-server): configure custom port to avoid permission issues (#23)\n\nUpdated webpack-dev-server scripts to run on port 4200 instead of default privileged ports.\n\nThis prevents EACCES permission errors when attempting to bind to port 443 on Unix-based systems without elevated privileges.\n\nChanges:\n\n* Added --port 4200 to start and cdev scripts\n* Ensures local development runs without requiring sudo\n\nNotes:\n\n* Keeps development environment aligned with common frontend defaults (e.g., Angular CLI)\n* Avoids conflicts with HTTPS/SSL reserved ports\n\n* feat(workspace): migrate frontend to Nx monorepo and pnpm workspaces\n\nThis migration restructures the Restaurante.Frontend project into a\nscalable monorepo using Nx and pnpm. The legacy AngularJS application\nhas been moved to a dedicated application directory to allow for\nfuture development and shared library support.\n\nKey changes:\n- Infrastructure: Initialized Nx workspace (nx.json) and pnpm workspaces.\n- Legacy App: Moved AngularJS source to apps/legacy-angularjs/ and\n  added project.json with Nx targets.\n- Dependency Management: Migrated to pnpm with a new root package.json.\n- Configuration: Set up tsconfig.base.json and updated .gitignore.\n- Tooling: Added AI agent guidelines (AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md) and MCP\n  server configuration.\n\n* feat: update project structure and clean up deprecated files\n\nRefactored the frontend structure to improve organization and maintainability.\nMoved and renamed key files to better align with the current architecture.\n\nRemoved deprecated AngularJS-related configurations and unused files.\nAdded new documentation files (AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md) for better project context.\n\nUpdated .gitignore to reflect the current development setup.\n\nThis change prepares the codebase for future improvements and a smoother migration process.\n\n* Introduces a comprehensive set of portable AI agent skills and\nconfigurations to enable autonomous workspace management.\n\nKey changes:\n- Added agent skills for core Nx operations: link-workspace-packages,\n  nx-generate, nx-import, and nx-workspace exploration.\n- Integrated the Monitor CI skill with self-healing capabilities\n  coordinated via Nx Cloud and the Model Context Protocol (MCP).\n- Configured subagent definitions for Claude, Codex, and OpenCode\n  environments to support multi-agent CI status tracking.\n- Updated opencode.json and .claude settings to register the\n  nx-mcp local server.\n- Added deterministic decision scripts (ci-poll-decide, ci-state-update)\n  for autonomous CI failure analysis and local fix application.\n\n* feat(restaurante): implement module federation to bridge legacy angularjs and v2\n\n- Infrastructure: Configured ModuleFederationPlugin in both the legacy AngularJS app (Webpack) and the new restaurante-v2 (Rspack).\n- Legacy Integration: Refactored legacy entry point to expose a mount function for manual bootstrapping.\n- Host Configuration: Created LegacyHostComponent in restaurante-v2 to dynamically import and mount the remote v1 app.\n- Routing: Updated app.routes to handle new v2 paths while defaulting all other traffic to the legacy host.\n- Dev Server: Adjusted ports (4201) and added proxy settings to handle legacy assets and views from the new host.\n- DX: Added remotes.d.ts for type safety when importing the legacy module.\n\n* feat(restaurante): implement module federation and fix legacy asset loading\n\n- Infrastructure: Configured ModuleFederationPlugin in both legacy (Webpack) and v2 (Rspack) to enable micro-frontend architecture.\n- Legacy Integration: Refactored entry point to export a mount function and implemented CORS headers in Webpack to allow cross-origin requests from the host.\n- Asset Resolution: Updated RequestInterceptorFN to use absolute URLs for templates and dynamic CSS, ensuring they are fetched from the legacy origin (port 4201).\n- Host Configuration: Created LegacyHostComponent in restaurante-v2 to dynamically import and bootstrap the remote legacy application.\n- Routing: Configured app.routes to prioritize new v2 paths while providing a wildcard fallback to the legacy host component.\n- Environment: Added LEGACY_PUBLIC_BASE_URL to manage asset origins and provided type definitions for the remote module to ensure DX and type safety.\n\n* refactor: modernize global scope usage and improve asset path resolution\n\n- Switch from ''global'' to ''globalThis'' for better environment compatibility\n- Refactor QuerieURLFromObject into a private class method within services\n- Implement regex-based asset path rewriting in RequestInterceptor\n- Update mount function to inject core application structure into the DOM\n- Fix TypeScript static $inject syntax in services\n\n* feat: dynamically load assets and dependencies on mount\n\nRefactor the entry point to ensure required stylesheets and scripts\nare present in the DOM before initializing the AngularJS module.\n\nChanges include:\n- Added `getPublicBaseUrl` to handle environment-specific asset paths.\n- Implemented `ensureLink` and `ensureScript` helpers to prevent\n  duplicate resource loading.\n- Updated `mount` to be asynchronous to wait for Bootstrap JS and\n  other critical assets.\n- Externalized Bootstrap and bundle CSS/JS loading to support\n  standalone or micro-frontend integration.","tree":{"sha":"7c8dd24d36208af2ccbf8f7a3e3550514c8cc502","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ariel-gallardo/restaurante/git/trees/7c8dd24d36208af2ccbf8f7a3e3550514c8cc502"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ariel-gallardo/restaurante/git/commits/67bc76ea6af87ecc6afcce965f053456cf293472","verification":{"payload":"tree 7c8dd24d36208af2ccbf8f7a3e3550514c8cc502\nparent e1e5d13e85394183820b8ab77caa26db2eb34cdd\nauthor Ariel Gallardo <38444032+ariel-gallardo@users.noreply.github.com> 1776190732 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776190732 -0300\n\nFeat/nx angular (#24)\n\n* feat(dev-server): configure custom port to avoid permission issues (#23)\n\nUpdated webpack-dev-server scripts to run on port 4200 instead of default privileged ports.\n\nThis prevents EACCES permission errors when attempting to bind to port 443 on Unix-based systems without elevated privileges.\n\nChanges:\n\n* Added --port 4200 to start and cdev scripts\n* Ensures local development runs without requiring sudo\n\nNotes:\n\n* Keeps development environment aligned with common frontend defaults (e.g., Angular CLI)\n* Avoids conflicts with HTTPS/SSL reserved ports\n\n* feat(workspace): migrate frontend to Nx monorepo and pnpm workspaces\n\nThis migration restructures the Restaurante.Frontend project into a\nscalable monorepo using Nx and pnpm. The legacy AngularJS application\nhas been moved to a dedicated application directory to allow for\nfuture development and shared library support.\n\nKey changes:\n- Infrastructure: Initialized Nx workspace (nx.json) and pnpm workspaces.\n- Legacy App: Moved AngularJS source to apps/legacy-angularjs/ and\n  added project.json with Nx targets.\n- Dependency Management: Migrated to pnpm with a new root package.json.\n- Configuration: Set up tsconfig.base.json and updated .gitignore.\n- Tooling: Added AI agent guidelines (AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md) and MCP\n  server configuration.\n\n* feat: update project structure and clean up deprecated files\n\nRefactored the frontend structure to improve organization and maintainability.\nMoved and renamed key files to better align with the current architecture.\n\nRemoved deprecated AngularJS-related configurations and unused files.\nAdded new documentation files (AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md) for better project context.\n\nUpdated .gitignore to reflect the current development setup.\n\nThis change prepares the codebase for future improvements and a smoother migration process.\n\n* Introduces a comprehensive set of portable AI agent skills and\nconfigurations to enable autonomous workspace management.\n\nKey changes:\n- Added agent skills for core Nx operations: link-workspace-packages,\n  nx-generate, nx-import, and nx-workspace exploration.\n- Integrated the Monitor CI skill with self-healing capabilities\n  coordinated via Nx Cloud and the Model Context Protocol (MCP).\n- Configured subagent definitions for Claude, Codex, and OpenCode\n  environments to support multi-agent CI status tracking.\n- Updated opencode.json and .claude settings to register the\n  nx-mcp local server.\n- Added deterministic decision scripts (ci-poll-decide, ci-state-update)\n  for autonomous CI failure analysis and local fix application.\n\n* feat(restaurante): implement module federation to bridge legacy angularjs and v2\n\n- Infrastructure: Configured ModuleFederationPlugin in both the legacy AngularJS app (Webpack) and the new restaurante-v2 (Rspack).\n- Legacy Integration: Refactored legacy entry point to expose a mount function for manual bootstrapping.\n- Host Configuration: Created LegacyHostComponent in restaurante-v2 to dynamically import and mount the remote v1 app.\n- Routing: Updated app.routes to handle new v2 paths while defaulting all other traffic to the legacy host.\n- Dev Server: Adjusted ports (4201) and added proxy settings to handle legacy assets and views from the new host.\n- DX: Added remotes.d.ts for type safety when importing the legacy module.\n\n* feat(restaurante): implement module federation and fix legacy asset loading\n\n- Infrastructure: Configured ModuleFederationPlugin in both legacy (Webpack) and v2 (Rspack) to enable micro-frontend architecture.\n- Legacy Integration: Refactored entry point to export a mount function and implemented CORS headers in Webpack to allow cross-origin requests from the host.\n- Asset Resolution: Updated RequestInterceptorFN to use absolute URLs for templates and dynamic CSS, ensuring they are fetched from the legacy origin (port 4201).\n- Host Configuration: Created LegacyHostComponent in restaurante-v2 to dynamically import and bootstrap the remote legacy application.\n- Routing: Configured app.routes to prioritize new v2 paths while providing a wildcard fallback to the legacy host component.\n- Environment: Added LEGACY_PUBLIC_BASE_URL to manage asset origins and provided type definitions for the remote module to ensure DX and type safety.\n\n* refactor: modernize global scope usage and improve asset path resolution\n\n- Switch from ''global'' to ''globalThis'' for better environment compatibility\n- Refactor QuerieURLFromObject into a private class method within services\n- Implement regex-based asset path rewriting in RequestInterceptor\n- Update mount function to inject core application structure into the DOM\n- Fix TypeScript static $inject syntax in services\n\n* feat: dynamically load assets and dependencies on mount\n\nRefactor the entry point to ensure required stylesheets and scripts\nare present in the DOM before initializing the AngularJS module.\n\nChanges include:\n- Added `getPublicBaseUrl` to handle environment-specific asset paths.\n- Implemented `ensureLink` and `ensureScript` helpers to prevent\n  duplicate resource loading.\n- Updated `mount` to be asynchronous to wait for Bootstrap JS and\n  other critical assets.\n- Externalized Bootstrap and bundle CSS/JS loading to support\n  standalone or micro-frontend integration.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp3oUMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATc4QAEybgLOZDrC55Hk00+/corpF\n0kkJvE2dklf2AACJv4SpTL/Knqe2jQK9AdaK+GUY+F5OF1HDR9lIW35QtXfF/Ojt\nYEE8K1klqJ8GYD7t93aymj+IW2jvH0XIMVY5I67DD9z5x12aYNQ0t2gCHbdEK0aJ\nQfmIq/VjUnr/RBnxIISICzUD5FZKsAWM3TJBeVEWKKaW7HBwdnBy1HoxbTb2aof4\n5vi7Shnshm2wTHdXdKOZ03k8/6zwJf7RvxSOQ/8EvkXJc3QbQhF/toFVH6jzoAWo\nXqQJahIVt7tGeNNQ+NyP1WX7Rmnsp4+DFmSq3wA7BxrME/cc5BD4MzG52L9hADzK\nqx0cT07OTy40KrDrTtYF3Nfa0I9apMNViXK+tlOS5A3+TWyM2IYpJXZ1U/YCSyUQ\nKbYkyJMRjgWRB4Kn+PnmH7RF0dYlrWt237az3dL6D9NAXgQcGS32gFQztO+m/WGe\nSFiW3vIx9Kygm23wLcYYbn1yh0ebS9HeLgBU2bTvgVS54GCph7z4EKNX5THFYuys\nV0FZ+uO5+SE2KfSbGQGcViT1t/GSR8Rwb3rQUFT/85GSL930SXpxHZI24m+h7dmo\nEmnimnXBdfAdVO0FJTvnQ6+fNO5qRFO0QJa6khlxCewTjqdBqd4Ot/iy+oCqSXPL\nJ6VNgKpTIOPfBIixOB+g\n=83GO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-14T18:18:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","grava